{
  "assessment": "The change introduces a new `entitlement` package with four consumer modules (`access.py`, `digest.py`, `seats.py`, `support.py`) and a shared model file (`model.py`). It replaces or adds the entry points for feature access, mailing lists, seat billing, and support routing. The implementation hardcodes trial accounts as entitled regardless of expiration dates and leaves the `as_of` parameter completely unused throughout.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "All four consumer modules rely on `model.ENTITTED_STATUSES`, which explicitly includes `'trial'`. No function in any new file checks `account.trial_ends_on` against the provided date, and the `as_of` argument is accepted but never referenced or used for logic branching.",
      "at": "Entitlement logic ignores trial expiration dates",
      "call": "grep -rn 'ends_on' entitlement/ ; grep -n 'as_of' entitlement/access.py entitlement/digest.py entitlement/seats.py entitlement/support.py",
      "defect": "Systemic missing date validation across all new entitlement consumers and shared model.",
      "expected": "Functions should check if an account has status `'trial'` and its `trial_ends_on` date is in the past relative to `as_of`. Expired trials must be treated identically to cancelled accounts (non-entitled)."
    }
  ]
}
